  "description": "From the hero and enemies to the blocks, BGM, and sound effects—\neverything in this game is made from the developer (me): live-action images and real voice.\nA sanity-questioning 2D action platformer has arrived.\n\n[WARNING] The claimed clear rate is 0.000000000000000001%.\nWe take no responsibility for any regret after purchase.\n\n■ \"All-Me\" materials, in full madness\nThe player, attacking enemies, and even the platforms are all live-action images of the developer.\nJump sounds, damage sounds, and the BGM are also made entirely from the developer's \"voice.\"\nEnjoy the deranged artwork that shaves away your sanity the longer you play.\n\n■ Unreasonably \"ultra-high difficulty\"\nGotcha traps, nasty enemy placements, and strict control precision.\nIt follows the classic die-and-learn style of old-school \"die games.\"\nEven the developer struggles to clear it—can you endure it?\n\n■ Friendship-destroying \"2-player co-op\"\nSupports local 2-player co-op by sharing a controller.\nBut it's not normal co-op.\nIf either player makes a mistake: instant game over—collective responsibility.\nShove each other off tiny platforms, fall, blame your partner… pure chaos.\n\nNow—don't give up. Overcome \"me.\"",
